        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-22T18:25:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAICT, mandoline is actually wrong on CPU today, and the results change with this CL, but even with the upcoming fix -- it\u0027s still broken (just different). Today, the deferred blitting code actually asserts if I make the edge sorting fix (because there is data stashed on the edge itself).",
      "parentUuid": "5748b6bb_3aae3c7d",
      "revId": "56273437ea66d1e8bd7d8f9fcf3d70620fb98191",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cdd30203_654265ef",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-22T18:27:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is to say, it appears that currently the \"deferred\" mode seems to (at least in some cases) currently be making things better than if it isn\u0027t used, it appears by logically combining areas instead of adding up the disjoint coverages (when possible, and things get complex when they aren\u0027t detected to logically combine, which I assume is the bug on its side). I\u0027m assuming the issue to be fixed with the non-deferred mode is to fix adding up the coverages?",
      "parentUuid": "5748b6bb_3aae3c7d",
      "revId": "56273437ea66d1e8bd7d8f9fcf3d70620fb98191",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "110c5d90_aa7eb6f1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-22T18:29:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, ok, so `mandoline` is probably a good torture test for this in general, and we still haven\u0027t quite figured it out. Then I suppose it\u0027s fine to stash this \"deferred\" code in the past and fix things up until `mandoline` does work, then if someone wants to resurrect the logic they have a good test.",
      "parentUuid": "cdd30203_654265ef",
      "revId": "56273437ea66d1e8bd7d8f9fcf3d70620fb98191",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f47e3ee6_86af4712",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-22T18:31:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Mostly I was just concerned that while `mandoline` isn\u0027t currently correct on CPU, this change by itself appears to make it even more incorrect.",
      "parentUuid": "110c5d90_aa7eb6f1",
      "revId": "56273437ea66d1e8bd7d8f9fcf3d70620fb98191",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
